{"term":"spit","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:0f2fd54c0eb99a9f24","definition":"A thin metal or wooden rod on which meat is skewered for cooking, often over a fire.","example":"They roaſt a fowl, by running a piece of wood through it, by way of ſpit, and holding it over a briſk fire, until the feathers are burnt of, when it is ready for eating, in their taſte.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["broach"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["sandspit","spitbraai","spit cake","spit engine","Spithead","spit jack","spit of land","turnspit","unspit","spitless"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spit#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a23e102f5fa483f6f0","definition":"A generally low, narrow, pointed, usually sandy peninsula or bar.","example":"Sand-spits are unfinished beaches, and long tongues or points of land, formed of sand and shingle, by the transporting action of currents and the waves. In Coldspring harbor, a sand-spit extends from the west shore, obliquely, nearly across. [...] The materials are transported by the currents and waves, and deposited to form this spit.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["sandspit","spitbraai","spit cake","spit engine","Spithead","spit jack","spit of land","turnspit","unspit","spitless"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spit#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c3ffaab8f7960613a9","definition":"To impale on a spit; to pierce with a sharp object.","example":"to spit a loin of veal","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["sandspit","spitbraai","spit cake","spit engine","Spithead","spit jack","spit of land","turnspit","unspit","spitless"],"source":"English W